\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
\
what is the diagnostic tool?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
for your convenience, the on-board frequency-matching engine is a simple and quick way to help pinpoint your specific tinnitus frequency.\
\
this is not meant to replace a proper diagnosis by a qualified medical professional, but it is provided for your exploration and understanding.\
\
the diagnostic tool section can be invoked from the bottom control bar. \
\
clicking \'93start test\'94 will load the test tone page, where you can preview all possible tinnitus frequencies.  once you\'92ve identified the general \'91range\'92, then you can click the yellow blinking arrow to expand the list to narrow down your search.    Continue auditioning until you find the one you feel is closest to matching the pitch of your internal ringing.  \
\
NOTE: experiment with different tone durations and volumes.  playing shorter bursts can often help to identify the correct pitch frequency.\
\
also NOTE:  when the correct frequency is played, \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
\ul \ulc2 you may experience\kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
\ulnone  a short term/momentary relief of your ringing.  this is a common occurrence, and can be an excellent way to identify your specific frequency.  letting the player continue for a minute or more may extend the relief period.\
