\f1\fs54 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
what is frequency-notching?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
in some cases, long-term or permanent relief can be achieved with notching therapy.  this is when the patient/user listens to audio content (in headphones/earbuds) where their specific tinnitus frequency band has been notched out. \
\
over time, the brain fills in the missing frequency and the internal ringing can be suppressed.  the recommended duration is: 1-2 hours daily for 2-3 weeks.\
\
in the diagnostic pages, once you pinpoint your tinnitus frequency, you can choose to notch out that frequency.  settings will be remembered, and you can reset at any time by simply going back to the test page and clicking \'91reset\'92 next to that frequency.\
\
further research is needed and this is not intended to replace professional medical consultation or treatment. \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
what is frequency-boosting?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
same as frequency-notching (above), except the pinpointed frequency is added/boosted louder, rather than subtracted/removed. You may find that boosting can be piercing at higher volumes, so you may have to listen, overall, quieter.\
\
these are the exact opposite therapies, but both have had positive reports.  frequency notching has been studied more.\
\
Reminder: neither of these therapies will be effective unless you listen with headphones or ear buds.\kerning1\expnd7\expndtw37
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
